# CadBridge byte-integrity rules.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Evidence artifacts carry SHA-256 hashes recorded in docs/evidence/**/manifest.json.
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default, and what this repo was created under),
# Git rewrites CRLF -> LF when storing a blob, so a fresh clone gets DIFFERENT bytes than
# the ones the manifest hashed. The manifest then appears to fail verification for no
# reason, and "verify the evidence" becomes meaningless.
#
# Therefore: evidence and tooling are stored EXACTLY as produced. No EOL conversion.
# Text normalization is only safe where the byte identity is not itself the evidence.

# Evidence bytes are the evidence. Never normalize.
docs/evidence/**  -text
*.jsonl           -text

# Command scripts fed verbatim to AutoCAD/accoreconsole (NETLOAD + command lines).
# A trailing newline and exact line endings are load-bearing here.
*.scr             -text

# Windows-native scripts.
*.ps1             text eol=crlf
*.cmd             text eol=crlf
*.bat             text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF to run under Git Bash / MSYS.
*.sh              text eol=lf

# C# and project files: normal text handling is fine.
*.cs              text
*.csproj          text
*.props           text

# Binary artifacts.
*.dll             binary
*.pdb             binary
*.dwg             binary
